From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp: Implement _Xoverflow_error, _Future_error_map and get_new_handler.

Exception helpers that were spec stubs: _Xoverflow_error, which throws a
std::overflow_error (a new class: runtime_error's layout, its own vtable,
RTTI and C++ type info; msvcp100 and later); _Future_error_map and
_Get_future_error_what, the message of a future_errc value (0-based in
msvcp110, 1-based in msvcp120, as future_error::what already counts); and
std::get_new_handler (the handler std::set_new_handler keeps; msvcp110,
msvcp120, msvcp140 on every architecture as <new> imports it, msvcp_win
forwards).
---
